Z||000000||Gokart||06-12-2000||09:45 PM||||....sends the temp so I'll get the reading on my gauge? Where is it located? I always assumed my GT ran cool cause it never got over 1/4 but now it's pegged at the bottom(far left) even if it's idleing for quite a while. In other words, I think it's time to change this sensor cause I'm getting no reading! TIA for replies <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||My7Fieros||06-12-2000||09:52 PM||||Well theres two sensors. The one that controls the guage is...I BELIEVE, but not quite positive, is around the distributor (if its a 6 cylinder)..theres another (coolant sensor) on the opposite side under the thermostat housing.....||||reg||1
Z||000002||Heisenhund||06-13-2000||04:46 AM||||Here's a simple check of your sensor, which is located right near the distributor on a V6. Pull the connection going to the sensor, and short the green wire to ground. If your gauge goes to the HIGH peg, your wiring is good, sensor bad. If it stays on the LOW peg then your wiring or gauge may be fouled up.<P>Heis<BR>||||reg||2
Z||000003||Heisenhund||06-13-2000||04:49 AM||||BTW there's actually 3 temperature sensors on the V6. One for the gauge, one for the ECM and one for the radfiator fan. The 2 not associated with temperature indication are located over near the thermostat housing.<P>Heis<BR>||||reg||1
